---
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
---

<section class="section" id="about" data-accent="coral">
  <div class="wrap reveal">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h2>A scientist working at the start of life.</h2>

    <div class="prose">
      <p class="lead">
        {SITE.name} is a developmental neuroscientist and stem cell biologist. She builds
        human models of the developing brain to learn what goes wrong in disease, and to find
        treatments that reach patients sooner.
      </p>
      <p>
        Her path runs from Delhi to Pune to Stanford. She earned her PhD in neuroscience at
        IISER Pune, where she studied how the nervous system wires itself, using zebrafish to
        watch growing neurons make their connections. In 2022 she moved to Stanford, where she
        now works in the Department of Pediatrics on the human brain at its earliest stages.
      </p>
      <p>
        What drives her is simple and stubborn: science should change real lives. She is drawn
        to the youngest and most vulnerable patients, to questions that sit at the edge of what
        we can model, and to the people she gets to teach and lift along the way.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
